# Units this rootfs MASKS — `build-rootfs.sh` symlinks each to
# /dev/null under /etc/systemd/system/, which is what
# `systemctl mask` does at runtime but applied at build time so the
# squashfs is the source of truth.
#
# A "mask" is stronger than "disable": a masked unit cannot be
# re-enabled mid-boot, even by a sloppy first-boot cloud-init runcmd.
#
# Rationale per unit:
#   rsyslog.service        — duplicates journald; journald keeps logs
#                            in /run/log/journal (tmpfs) so they don't
#                            persist past poweroff (§20 logging
#                            discipline). rsyslog would re-stream to
#                            /var/log/* which adds disk pressure on
#                            the small data volume + non-deterministic
#                            file mtimes.
#   cron.service           — no scheduled jobs in a serverless tenant
#                            baseline; mask avoids the daily
#                            `cron.daily` runs touching state.
#   getty@*.service        — no TTY in a serverless CVM. The QEMU
#                            serial console is reserved for kernel
#                            diagnostics; an interactive login on it
#                            would defeat the no-shell §20 posture.
#   apt-daily.service +
#   apt-daily-upgrade.service — the rootfs is dm-verity (read-only at
#                              runtime). Apt updates would either
#                              fail noisily (writing to a read-only
#                              FS) OR succeed quietly on an overlay
#                              and drift away from the measured
#                              image. Mask both.
#   systemd-timesyncd      — an NTP query before NetBird is up would
#                            block, AND the host's SEV-SNP attestable
#                            RTC is already the trust anchor for time
#                            inside the CVM. Skip.
#   serial-getty@*.service — same posture as getty@*; the ttyS0
#                            console is for diagnostics only.
#
# This file is consumed by `build-rootfs.sh::mask_units`. Format:
# one unit per line, blank lines + `#` comments ignored.

rsyslog.service
cron.service
getty@tty1.service
getty@tty2.service
getty@tty3.service
getty@tty4.service
getty@tty5.service
getty@tty6.service
serial-getty@ttyS0.service
apt-daily.service
apt-daily-upgrade.service
apt-daily.timer
apt-daily-upgrade.timer
systemd-timesyncd.service
